Package: com.huhansibuxin.cachedeletequiet
Name: CacheDeleteQuiet
Version: 1.1.1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: PLAN D: kills the 80-99% CPU spikes of CacheDeleteAppContainerCaches by rebinding, inside that one XPC helper process, the arm64e auth-GOT slots of the recursive C scans (_fast_size_directory / _traverse_directory). An fs_usage spike capture proved the CPU is spent on per-file open+fstat64+getattrlistbulk+close walks over App container tmp/trash, and v1.0.1 logs proved none of the ObjC selectors are on that path. Real PURGE (_CacheManagementEnumerateAssets / _CacheManagementRemove), _statfs, the XPC listener and all replies are untouched. v1.1.1 fixes v1.0/1.1.0 using dyld image 0 as the main executable (roothide can put an injected dylib there): all three slots read 0 and bound=0/3 on device. Now locates the helper image by name + dladdr cross-check and derives slot addresses from its real LC_SEGMENT_64 layout, with full image/segment/slot diagnostics. No PAC signature is guessed: each slot's dyld-signed pointer is numerically self-verified first and left alone on any mismatch (fail-open). Disabling the daemon is NOT used because that breaks app launches. Flags in /var/mobile/Documents/CacheDeleteQuiet/ (or /var/tmp): PROBE_ONLY (rebind but call original, A/B baseline), PASSTHROUGH_ALL (no rebind), STRICT, DISABLED; touch then kickstart -k. No substrate/ellekit/Foundation link, no Logos, no timers, no polling.
Maintainer: huhansibuxin
Author: huhansibuxin
Section: Tweaks
Depends: ellekit
